::Q1::What does a testing framework provide beyond manually writing assert statements and calling test functions? 
{
=Automated test discovery, execution, and reporting
~Automatic correction of bugs in the application
~A replacement for all application code
~Only a faster Python interpreter
}

::Q2::Which statement about unittest is correct? 
{
=It is included with Python's standard library
~It must always be installed with pip
~It only supports plain test functions
~It cannot report failed assertions
}

::Q3::How are tests commonly organized in unittest? 
{
=As methods inside a class that inherits from unittest.TestCase
~As database records inside a test server
~As functions inside a class that does not inherit from anything
~As shell commands with no Python code
}

::Q4::Which unittest assertion method checks that two values are equal? 
{
=assertEqual(a, b)
~assertSame(a, b)
~assertMatch(a, b)
~assertEqualsOnly(a, b)
}

::Q5::What naming convention allows unittest to recognize a method as a test? 
{
=The method name starts with test_
~The method name ends with _testcase
~The method name contains unittest
~The method name must be named test only
}

::Q6::How is pytest commonly installed? {
=pip install pytest
~python install unittest
~pip install unittest
~pytest install python
}

::Q7::Which file pattern is automatically discovered by pytest? {
=test_*.py
~only_tests.py
~pytest_only.py
~run_tests.txt
}

